      "units": [
        {
          "id": "s0166",
          "zh": "文多不載。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "The text is extensive and is not recorded here.",
              "idiomatic": "The compilation ran long and is omitted here.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0167",
          "zh": "武帝楊悼皇后既母養懷帝，后遇難時，懷帝尚幼，及即位，中詔述后恩愛。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "Empress Yang Dao of Emperor Wu had already mother-nurtured Emperor Huai; when she later met violent death, Emperor Huai was still young; when he ascended, an inner edict recounted the empress's kindness and love.",
              "idiomatic": "Empress Yang had raised the future Emperor Huai; when she was killed he was still a child, and on enthronement he issued a palace rescript praising her care.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0168",
          "zh": "及后祖載，群官議帝應為追制服，或以庶母慈己，依禮制小功五月，或以謂慈母服如母服齊衰者，眾議不同。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "When later her funeral train departed, the many offices debated whether the emperor ought wear retroactive mourning—or some said because a concubine-mother had loved him, by ritual he should wear xiao gong five months—or some said foster-mother mourning like a mother's qi-cui—the many opinions differed.",
              "idiomatic": "At her cortège the ministries split: some wanted retroactive weeds, some cited a nurturing concubine's xiao gong, some equated her to a legal mother in qi-cui.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0169",
          "zh": "閭丘沖議云：「楊后母養聖上，蓋以曲情。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "Luqiu Chong debated: 'Empress Yang mother-nurtured the sage ascendant—generally out of special affection.",
              "idiomatic": "Luqiu Chong debated: 'Empress Yang mother-nurtured the sage ascendant—generally out of special affection.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0170",
          "zh": "今以恩禮追崇，不配世祖廟。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "Now by kindness and ritual we posthumously honor her—not pairing her in Emperor Shizu's temple.",
              "idiomatic": "Now by kindness and ritual we posthumously honor her—not pairing her in Emperor Shizu's temple.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0171",
          "zh": "王者無慈養之服，謂宜祖載之日，可三朝素服發哀而已。」",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "For kings there is no garment for 'foster nurturing'; I say on the day of the funeral train, three court sessions in plain dress to raise mourning is enough.'",
              "idiomatic": "For kings there is no garment for 'foster nurturing'; I say on the day of the funeral train, three court sessions in plain dress to raise mourning is enough.'",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
