      "units": [
        {
          "id": "s0201",
          "zh": "漢之光武，不嗣于孝成，而上承於元帝。』",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "Han Guangwu does not succeed Xiaocheng but receives above from Emperor Yuan.",
              "idiomatic": "Han's Guangwu does not follow Xiaocheng but inherits from Emperor Yuan.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2.5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0202",
          "zh": "又曰：『晉惠帝無後，懷帝承統，懷帝自繼于世祖，而不繼于惠帝。",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "Also: 'Jin Emperor Hui had no heir; Emperor Huai received the succession; Huai succeeded himself from Shizu, not from Emperor Hui.",
              "idiomatic": "Jin Hui had no heir; Huai took the line from Shizu, not from Hui.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2.5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s0203",
          "zh": "其惠帝當同陽甲、孝成，別出為廟。』",
          "translations": [
            {
              "lang": "en",
              "literal": "Emperor Hui should be the same as Yang Jia and Xiaocheng, separately enshrined outside.",
              "idiomatic": "Hui should join Yang Jia and Xiaocheng in a separate shrine.",
              "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
              "model": "Composer 2.5"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "primaryTempleNameDefinition": {
    "book": "jinshu",
    "chapter": "003",
    "units": [
      {
        "id": "s0001",
        "zh": "武皇帝諱炎，字安世，文帝長子也。",
        "translations": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "literal": "The Martial Emperor's taboo name was Yan, his style name Anshi; he was the eldest son of Emperor Wen.",
            "idiomatic": "The emperor honored posthumously as Wu bore the personal name Yan and the courtesy name Anshi; he was the firstborn son of Emperor Wen (Sima Zhao).",
            "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
            "model": "Composer 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s0636",
        "zh": "己酉，帝崩于含章殿，時年五十五，葬峻陽陵，廟號世祖。",
        "translations": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "literal": "On the day jiyou the emperor died in the Hanzhang hall at age fifty-five; he was buried at Junyang mausoleum with temple name Shizu.",
            "idiomatic": "Jiyou: the emperor expired in Hanzhang at fifty-five, buried at the Junyang tomb with the temple name Shizu.",
            "translator": "Garrett M. Petersen (2026)",
            "model": "Composer 2"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
